Privacy Policy — Lucifer bot
Last updated: 2026-08-26

This is the public copy of the policy that members can also read inside the server with !privacy. Both are kept in sync; if they ever differ, this page is the authoritative one.

Who we are
The Friendscord bot is a private Discord bot operated by the moderation team of the Friendscord Discord server. It runs only in that server and is not available for use anywhere else. It is not listed in any bot directory and has no public invite.

Contact for data questions: support@matchflow.gg

What the bot processes
Messages posted in the server's public channels, including text, attachments and links.
Your Discord user ID, username and avatar.
Server data such as your roles, your join date and your account creation date.
Voice channel join and leave events.
Moderation records created by the moderation team.
The bot does not read your private conversations. The only direct messages it sees are ones sent to the bot itself.

Why
Message content is screened automatically so that content prohibited by our rules — sexual content, NSFW images, harassment, hate speech, doxxing, encouragement of self harm, scams and spam — can be removed quickly, and so the bot can read the text commands moderators use.

Member data is used to welcome new members, assign roles, apply and lift punishments, and judge proportionality before any automated action: a brand new throwaway account and a longstanding member are not treated the same.

Other features (roles, games, logging) use the same data for the purpose each feature plainly describes.

What we store, and for how long
On a private server controlled by the moderation team, the bot stores:

Discord user IDs.
Moderation records: date, acting moderator, reason, duration, and a short excerpt of the message concerned.
Role assignments made through the bot's role features.
Per server settings.
Moderation records are kept for [12 months] so punishments can be reviewed and appealed. We do not keep an archive of ordinary messages: a message that is never flagged is held briefly in memory for context and then discarded.

Automated screening and third parties
When a message is posted, its text — and any image attached to it, where relevant — is sent to [PROVIDER]'s API to be classified against our rules, and a decision is returned. We do not store the message with that provider. Under its API data policy, requests may be retained by the provider for up to 30 days for abuse monitoring and are not used to train its models.

No other third party receives data from this bot. We do not sell your data, share it for advertising, or use it to train any machine learning model of our own.

Automated decisions and appeals
The bot can delete messages and warn, mute, kick or ban accounts automatically. Every such action is logged with its reasoning, and every one of them can be reviewed and reversed by a human moderator.

To appeal an action, contact the moderation team https://discord.gg/Z2hC7jR

Your choices
Automated moderation cannot be switched off for individual members. It protects everyone in the server, including our youngest members, and it applies equally to staff and to the server owner. You can leave the server at any time, which ends all processing except retained moderation records.

You can ask for a copy of the data stored about you, or ask for it to be deleted, with !mydata whatdata and !mydata forgetme, or by contacting support@matchflow.gg We respond within 30 days. We may keep a minimal record of a ban, since deleting it would let a banned user return undetected.

Age
Discord requires users to be at least 13, or older where local law requires it. We do not knowingly process data belonging to anyone below that age, and we remove such accounts from the server when we become aware of them.

Security
Data is held on an access restricted server available only to the bot's administrators.

Changes
We update this policy when the bot's data handling changes, and the date at the top changes with it.
